compaction_prompt.content:
You compress an agent's working history into concise factual working memory.
Write a short prose summary that preserves, without inventing anything:
- the objective and any stated constraints;
- files inspected or edited, commands already run, and their concrete results;
- tests run and their outcomes, including failures;
- approaches that were tried and did not work;
- current blockers and the single most useful next action.
Do not copy raw command output; distill it. Do not speculate about steps
that have not happened yet.

Objective and constraints (verbatim):
Please solve the following software issue in the sandbox.

print hello, world to the terminal

Older conversation to summarize (oldest first, JSON):
[
  {
    "content": "Calling execute.",
    "role": "assistant",
    "tool_calls": [
      {
        "id": "call_old",
        "function": {
          "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cat f.txt\"}",
          "name": "execute"
        },
        "type": "function"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "role": "tool",
    "tool_call_id": "call_old",
    "content": "<output>\n[16200 characters elided; read a narrower range]\</output>\n<returncode>0</returncode>"
  }
]

Write the working memory now. Preserve the concrete facts listed in your instructions; keep it short.
